  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid Response Fund for Humanitarian Emergencies in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM has been managing the Rapid Response Programme in Sudan as one of the most effective, short term, and flexible funding mechanisms that offers sub-grants to and international and national non-governmental organizations (I/NNGOs) to respond to critical humanitarian needs that are triggered by natural or manmade disasters. Since 2014 to date, and in a close coordination with the Sectors and sub-sectors in targeted areas, the Rapid Response Fund (RRF) has awarded nearly 80 sub-grants worth more than USD 14 million to I/NNGOs in Sudan that have provided critical life-saving assistance to more than one million beneficiaries across Sudan in the following Sectors: Shelter and Settlements; Non-food Items (NFIs); Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH); Health; Food Security and Livelihoods (FSL); Protection; and Humanitarian Coordination and Information Management. To ensure the continued delivery of these vital, lifesaving, short-term projects, IOM Sudan is providing up to 30 grants and support nearly 700,000 vulnerable individuals over a period of 17 months.</narrative>
  </description>
